From 0114bcb47c18172991d1b87606f1bd475056de56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huhu233 <925393268@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:31:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui-subagent): show the model route each subagent ran on
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The catalog reported a child's mode, activity, usage, and duration but
never which model it actually ran on, so a delegation that pinned a
route was indistinguishable from one that inherited the parent's.

Rows now stack three lines — the child's name, a badge line carrying
mode, activity, and the route, and the log-backed title — which also
stops an over-long title from ellipsizing the badges away. A child
session's own header carries the same readout beside its breadcrumb
switcher, gated to the child sessions that renderer already owns.

The route comes from the existing durable `modelSelection` projection,
which already records the provider, model, and reasoning effort of each
`request/header`. Catalog rows read it from the summary's projection
values they already load for token usage and timing, so this adds no
RPC, no host surface, and no new slot.
